From fcfb9b27f53bfcd39103cc5e8c3c3ec8abb87b7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 18:39:14 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 11/60] TP RoCE: every RDMA post is bounds-checked before the
 verb, and peers with another region layout are refused

roce_guard.stripes computes each HCA's share of a post (its send stripe, the peer's receive range and its flag word)
and refuses with error.OutOfRegion any range past its slot, its flag area or the registered region, before
post_send. The verbs wire and the shm wire both post through it. The shm wire moves to roce_shm.zig and can stripe
like the verbs wire (Options.shm_stripes), with an optional tap that sees every post for tests. The connection record
carries the slot and registered length, so a peer with another layout is refused at connect; its magic is bumped.

Tests: stripes tile the slot over two HCAs and refuse a post past the slot, a third slot, an unpadded or empty post,
no HCA and a short region. On fake verbs a post past its slot reaches no verb, and a full slot stays inside the
region. Over the shm wire striped as two HCAs, 2,000 variable-length gathers stay inside slot and region, bit for bit.

(cherry picked from commit e16e331a087bb6e60d0d04854a4cdcc7c3f02ed0)
